Third-party components
======================

The MIT license in LICENSE covers this repository's own code. The following are not covered by
it and keep their own licenses.

kernel/Image
    A Linux kernel (GPL-2.0-only) with an initramfs containing BusyBox (GPL-2.0-only).
    Corresponding source:
      Linux 6.8-rc1, https://git.kernel.org/torvalds/t/linux-6.8-rc1.tar.gz
        sha256 327c0c2dcbe348ab9902dc30511f5cfb239cfff8a8d285b29779c4b5bd7c8e42
        patches, applied in order (kernel/patches/):
          0001-Experimental-RISC-V-32-bit-No-MMU-support.patch   from mini-rv32ima's buildroot
          0002-mini-rv32ima-HVC-driver.patch                     from mini-rv32ima's buildroot
          0003-riscv-skip-misaligned-probe-keep-init-text.patch  this project
        configuration: kernel/linux.config (generated by kernel/mkconfig.sh from kernel/config.orig)
      BusyBox 1.36.1, https://busybox.net/downloads/busybox-1.36.1.tar.bz2
        sha256 b8cc24c9574d809e7279c3be349795c5d5ceb6fdf19ca709f80cde50e47de314
        patches: userland/patches/ (buildroot's package/busybox patches)
        configuration: userland/busybox.config (generated by userland/build_busybox.sh)
      uClibc-ng 1.0.44 (LGPL-2.1), statically linked into the BusyBox binary,
        https://downloads.uclibc-ng.org/releases/1.0.44/uClibc-ng-1.0.44.tar.xz
        sha256 7df9d987955827382f1c2400da513456becbb6f868bdfd37737265f1cbeec994
        patches and configuration: package/uclibc/ of the buildroot commit below
        (built by its toolchain target; the complete BusyBox source above allows relinking)
      Toolchain: https://github.com/cnlohr/buildroot at 851edd247f5e2e8e10f943c52218bc54c657688f
        with the configs of https://github.com/cnlohr/mini-rv32ima at
        84858f58cb41899705e2ff2d6ee3b2d5c0795bfe
    Wherever the model's booted snapshot (which holds this Image and BusyBox) is distributed,
    the source tarballs above, with the patches and configurations, go with it (gpl-source/).
    Build: scripts/setup.sh, then KERNEL=1 scripts/setup.sh or kernel/build.sh. The build is
    reproducible: kernel/build.sh fixes the banner's user, host, time and build number
    (KBUILD_BUILD_*), and userland/build_busybox.sh fixes BusyBox's build date
    (SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH). Rebuilt from a fresh kernel tree and a fresh BusyBox build, the Image
    is identical to kernel/Image.

kernel/patches/, userland/patches/
    GPL-2.0-only, as the programs they patch.

